{"name":"Mud Bath","hex":"#7c6841","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mud bath","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The immersion of the body in mud, for therapeutic reasons.","A very muddy or dirty area or thing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mud_bath"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mud bath","blocks":[{"text":"A mud bath is a therapeutic treatment that involves soaking in a bath of warm mud, often in a natural hot spring or geothermal pool, inland sea or at a spa. Mud baths have been used for centuries as a way to promote health and relaxation, and are still popular today in many parts of the world. Mud baths can be found at spa resorts and hot springs, both natural and developed, globally."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Baie_cu_namol_-_Turcia_2006.jpg/330px-Baie_cu_namol_-_Turcia_2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mud_bath","wikidata":"Q304502"},{"title":"Mud","blocks":[{"text":"Mud is loam, silt, or clay mixed with water. Mud is usually formed after rainfall or near water sources. Ancient mud deposits hardened over geological time to form sedimentary rock such as shale or mudstone. When geological deposits of mud are formed in estuaries, the resultant layers are termed bay muds. Mud has also been used for centuries as a construction resource, mostly for houses, and also as a binder. An Old English word for it was fen, now in most dialects referring to a type of wetland."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/2003-11-27_Northerner_boots_in_mud.jpg/330px-2003-11-27_Northerner_boots_in_mud.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mud","wikidata":"Q170449"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Mud_baths_at_Saki_%288612609077%29.jpg/500px-Mud_baths_at_Saki_%288612609077%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Mud_baths_at_Saki_%288612609077%29.jpg/1280px-Mud_baths_at_Saki_%288612609077%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Mud_baths_at_Saki_%288612609077%29.jpg/500px-Mud_baths_at_Saki_%288612609077%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mud baths at Yevpatoria circa 1920","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMud_baths_at_Saki_(8612609077).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Pirgel_Mud_Volcano_13960604_11.jpg/500px-Pirgel_Mud_Volcano_13960604_11.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Pirgel_Mud_Volcano_13960604_11.jpg/500px-Pirgel_Mud_Volcano_13960604_11.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Person bathing in Pirgel Mud Volcano, Balochistan","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APirgel_Mud_Volcano_13960604_11.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/A_guy_enjoying_a_mud_bath_%282957458381%29.jpg/500px-A_guy_enjoying_a_mud_bath_%282957458381%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/A_guy_enjoying_a_mud_bath_%282957458381%29.jpg/1280px-A_guy_enjoying_a_mud_bath_%282957458381%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/A_guy_enjoying_a_mud_bath_%282957458381%29.jpg/500px-A_guy_enjoying_a_mud_bath_%282957458381%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Man mud bathing at the Dead Sea","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fi